<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82874" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πήγᾰνον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rue, Ruta graveolens</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diocl.Fr.
				138
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theopomp.Hist.
				177
			</span></i>(<i>a</i>), <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				127.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				1.3.4
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				413
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὀρεινόν, ἄγριον</span>,
				<i>mountain rue, Ruta halepensis</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.45
			</span></i> (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἄγριον,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶλυ</span>
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				46
			</span></i>) : prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἐν δελίνῳ οὐδ᾽ ἐν
				πηγάνῳ</span>, i.e. scarcely at the <i>edge</i> or
				<i>beginning</i> of a thing, because these herbs were planted
			for borders in gardens, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				480
			</span></i> ; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίκηπος</span>.</div>
